# Line endings are LF in the repository and must stay LF in every checkout.
# The suite compares fixture bytes, `include_str!` contents, and insta
# snapshots against output this tool writes with `\n`, so a checkout that
# rewrites them to CRLF — the default for Git for Windows — fails comparisons
# that have nothing to do with the change under test.
#
# `text=auto` keeps the detection Git already applies at commit time, so a
# binary file is left alone rather than normalized.
* text=auto eol=lf
